WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.580
Rhiannon: The emotional health
of children and young people is

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.780
increasingly recognised as being
fundamental to their wellbeing.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.090
As emotional health is nurtured
primarily in the home, as long as this

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.000
is a calm and loving environment, it
can only be positive for the future

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.310
prospects of individuals and communities.

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:21.750
Leah: The good emotional health of
children and young people is vital to

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.929
them as individuals, as being emotionally
healthy is an important end in itself

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.540
and is also linked with a range of
positive outcomes in later life.

00:00:31.219 --> 00:00:34.949
It does not necessarily mean being
happy all the time, but it does

00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:38.330
mean having the resilience to face
the challenges that occur in life.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.730
Rhiannon: The good emotional health
and well-being of children and young

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:46.550
people is also vital to society, as
poor mental health in children and

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:51.050
young people is associated with teenage
pregnancy, bullying, violent and

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.719
criminal behaviour and substance misuse.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:00:59.930
The majority of adults with mental
health problems experienced mental

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.480
health concerns in childhood.

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:06.000
These problems not only persist
through to adulthood but can also

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.949
have an impact the next generation.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.290
Leah: The development of emotional health
starts even before a child is born,

00:01:12.709 --> 00:01:16.429
with the first two years of life being
critical for putting in the foundations

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.290
for emotional health throughout childhood.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.520
This then follows onward into adult life,
through the parent to child relationship.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:27.139
Promoting the emotional health of
children and young people can be

00:01:27.139 --> 00:01:31.040
done by supporting friendships, peer
relationships and personal development,

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:35.170
within early years, school and college
settings and by providing additional

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.330
advice and support if problems arise.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.820
Rhiannon: Conduct disorders can be
difficult to diagnose, as some of

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.260
these troublesome behaviours can be
a result of environmental factors

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.549
or other mental health conditions.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.990
Leah: A child who has a poor emotional
environment with poor role models

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.870
may struggle to develop positive
relationships with their peers.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.019
They may fall behind academically and risk
later involvement in risky behaviours.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.000
They may also develop physical and mental
health issues in their adult life and are

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.900
unlikely to reach their full potential.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:12.570
A good emotional environment will
provide a secure base for children

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:16.609
to grow into well-rounded resilient
adults with good mental health.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.750
A child’s social and emotional development
is vital for their future, if they are

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.810
to achieve their full potential socially,
academically and career-wise as an adult.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.000
Strong bonds with a parent or carer
can help to develop a resilience to

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.059
stress, an ability to balance emotions
and enable the child to have meaningful

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.319
interpersonal relationships in the future.

